      "title": "The A site: where tRNAs come in",
      "narration": "The ribosome has three spots: E, P, and A. New tRNAs always come in at the A site. Each one carries an amino acid. Here's one that doesn't match. Its anticodon doesn't pair, so it leaves. Here's one that does. It pairs with the codon and stays. Like a key that only fits its own lock. A charged tRNA enters at the A site and stays if its anticodon matches the codon. Swipe.",
